mothershipOS: zero-copy NV12 capture and the per-stream work on the GPU (ExternalCameraGpu: EGL/GLES3).
A mothershipOS host offers NV12: the HAL allocates its own NV12 gralloc buffers, queues them as DMABUF (the host
renders each frame into them; the device takes their layout: bytesperline and the "nv12 scanlines" control), and
the GPU samples the capture buffer's planes (R8 / RG88 dma-buf images) to crop and scale them into each NV12/NV21
output buffer. YU12 on the CPU (NV12ToI420) only for JPEG, planar or Y16 outputs, or when the GPU path fails.
XBGR32 frames (MMAP): one upload, then crop + scale + BT.601 on the GPU. Properties:
ro.vendor.camera.external.dmabuf=false (MMAP capture), ro.vendor.camera.external.gpu=false (XBGR32, CPU path).

